# Cursor Rules for Flavories Web Client

## Project context
- React 19 + TypeScript (strict) with Vite; Joy UI is the primary component library.
- Theme and tokens live in `src/theme.ts`; keep colors/radii/typography sourced from `theme.vars` and Joy tokens rather than hardcoded values.
- Routing is defined in `src/routes/routes.tsx` and rendered via `AppRoutes`; `App` provides the fixed top nav and spacer offset — preserve this structure when adding pages.
- Global providers: `CssVarsProvider` + `CssBaseline`, `SnackbarProvider` (`useSnackbar` for toasts). Prefer these over ad‑hoc implementations.
- HTTP goes through `src/api/axiosClient.ts` (adds Bearer token from `localStorage`) and service wrappers in `src/services/**`. Reuse/extend services instead of calling `axios` directly.

## Code style
- Use functional components with explicit return types (`JSX.Element`); keep hooks at the top level, name custom hooks with `use*`.
- Favor `import type` for type‑only imports; avoid `any` and keep DTO types in `services/*/*.dto.ts` as the source of truth.
- Prefer Joy components and the `sx` prop for styling; keep spacing, radii, and colors aligned to the theme (`theme.vars.radius.*`, palette keys).
- Keep components small and focused; extract reusable UI into `src/components/` and shared logic into hooks/contexts.
- Handle errors gracefully (user‑facing feedback via `SnackbarProvider` or Joy `Alert`); don’t swallow async errors.

## UI / UX guidance
- Maintain the existing visual language: generous padding, rounded corners, soft shadows, and the orange/green brand accents from the theme palette.
- Default to accessible Joy variants (`variant="soft/solid/plain"`) and set `aria` labels when icons stand alone; ensure inputs/buttons remain keyboard navigable.
- Keep layouts responsive: use `Stack`, `Box`, and flex utilities; avoid fixed widths except where required (e.g., navbar height offset).
- Provide meaningful alt text for images (logo, recipe thumbnails, avatars fallback).
- Favor clear CTAs and inline validation messages; surface feedback via snackbars for transient events.

## Data & services
- Base API URL comes from `VITE_API_BASE_URL`; keep all calls relative and centralized through services.
- Auth token is stored in `localStorage` as `token`; preserve this contract when updating auth flows.
- When adding new endpoints, extend existing service modules and co‑locate request/response DTOs.

## Tooling & commands
- Package manager: `bun` preferred (lockfile present); `bun install`, `bun run dev`, `bun run lint`. If bun is unavailable, fall back to npm without changing lockfiles.
- Run `bun run lint` before shipping significant changes; format with Prettier defaults (no extra config present).

## Testing & quality
- No test suite yet; for new logic that’s complex, add lightweight unit/logic tests if infra allows, otherwise keep functions small and predictable.
- Watch for strict TypeScript warnings (`noUnused*`, `noFallthrough`, etc.) and fix at the source.

## Miscellaneous
- Keep new files ASCII; follow existing casing conventions (PascalCase components, camelCase utilities).
- Avoid introducing new global styles when a Joy token can handle it. If you must add globals, do so via `GlobalStyles` in `src/main.tsx`.

